WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.083
The method is evaluated on two settings.

00:00:04.163 --> 00:00:08.246
The first is a synthetic benchmark: a
two-dimensional mixture of three Gaussian clusters,

00:00:08.326 --> 00:00:12.409
where the target keeps the same clusters but
changes their proportions and shifts them in space,

00:00:12.489 --> 00:00:16.572
across three scenarios of increasing imbalance.

00:00:16.652 --> 00:00:20.735
The second is a real single-cell perturbation dataset,

00:00:20.815 --> 00:00:24.898
generated with the imaging technology called 4i,

00:00:24.978 --> 00:00:29.062
that tracks two co-cultured melanoma cell lines
responding to twenty-five different drugs.

00:00:29.142 --> 00:00:33.225
Cells are measured at zero, eight, and twenty-four hours,

00:00:33.305 --> 00:00:37.388
with control cells exposed only to a vehicle
serving as the source and the perturbed populations serving as targets.

00:00:37.468 --> 00:00:41.551
The two cell lines are distinguished by mutually
exclusive protein markers,

00:00:41.631 --> 00:00:45.714
MelA and Sox9,

00:00:45.794 --> 00:00:49.877
and additional markers for proliferation and cell
death allow the predicted mass changes

00:00:49.957 --> 00:00:54.040
to be checked against biology.
